+>## - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
+>##                          ComfyUI-ZImagePowerNodes
+>##     ComfyUI nodes designed to power the "Z-Image/Z-Image Turbo" models.
+>##_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _
+>##
+>## HOW TO WRITE A STYLE TEMPLATE
+>##    Focus exclusively on visual aesthetic, atmospheric mood, and technical
+>##    characteristics (e.g., lighting, texture, lens, weather, sensations,..).
+>##    Avoid mentioning specific subjects, objects, or characters, as these are
+>##    provided by the user via the {$@} variable. Think of the template as a
+>##    "lens" or "filter": it defines how the scene feels and looks, not what
+>##    is happening in it.
+>##
+>## TEMPLATE DEFINITION
+>##    Each new visual style must begin with a line prefixed with ">>>"
+>##    followed by the style name(*). Example: ">>> Landscape Photo"
+>##
+>## TEMPLATE FORMAT
+>##    Every line following the style name represents the prompt used
+>##    when that style is selected. The following variables are processed:
+>##
+>##    {$@} : Replaced by the user's input prompt.
+>##
+>##    {$IFPAL x | y} :
+>##         Conditional logic for color palettes.
+>##         - If a color palette is selected, the text 'x' is used.
+>##         - If no palette is selected, the text 'y' is used.
+>##         - Within 'x', use $1, $2, $3, and $4 to reference specific
+>##           colors from the palette.
+>##         - $5 is an optional highlight color (not available in all palettes).
+>##
+>##    {**<symbol-char> x | y} :
+>##         Quick Modifier (cheats).
+>##         - If the user's prompt is prefixed with the corresponding
+>##           cheat code, the text 'x' is used.
+>##         - If no cheat code prefix is detected, the text 'y' is used.
+>##
+>## (*)NOTE
+>## Style names are plain text strings that may include an optional variant
+>## separated by double slash (//). Example:">>>Vintage CRT // Arcade Cabinet"
+>##
+
+>############################ Classic Film Photo ############################
+
+>>> Classic Film Photo
+YOUR CONTEXT
+You are a master cinematographer specializing in the Golden Age of Hollywood (1950s-1960s).
+Your photographs possess a warm, nostalgic color temperature, fine-grain texture, motion blur, and subtle visual imperfections.
+The lighting is high-contrast with dramatic rim lighting.
+{$IFPAL
+The scene uses cinematic tones: shadows are rendered in $3, midtones in $2, and highlights in $1. |
+The scene features the timeless, authentic look of classic film, characterized by deep blacks, crisp whites, and the warm, weathered aesthetic of vintage cinema.
+}
+YOUR PHOTO:
+<!--
+{$@}
+-->
+
+>>> Classic Film Photo // Theatrical Set
+Your photographs capture the distinctive aesthetic of a classic 1950s soundstage, where the atmosphere is entirely artificial and tactile. The set design relies on painted backdrops, elaborate cardboard constructions, and forced perspective techniques. Distant elements are rendered as matte paintings on studio walls, creating an environment that feels completely artificial and theatrical.
+The images feature a warm, nostalgic color temperature, a fine-grained texture, and high-contrast lighting that emphasizes the deliberate artifice of the constructed world.
+
+The scene is defined by a controlled, staged perspective, where textures feel intentionally handcrafted, utilizing painted backgrounds and constructed set elements to evoke the charm and inherent artifice of period film sets.
+YOUR PHOTO:
+<!--
+{$@}
+-->
+
+>>> Classic Film Photo // Grand Epic Production
+YOUR CONTEXT
+You are a master cinematographer of the Golden Age of Hollywood, specializing in sweeping, large-scale epic productions.
+Your photographs possess a warm, nostalgic color temperature, evoking the distinct look of mid-century high-budget cinema. The image is rendered with the organic, velvety grain of 70mm large-format film, exhibiting a soft, golden-hued warmth and a subtle, honeyed amber patina characteristic of vintage celluloid.
+The lighting is expansive and majestic, utilizing powerful key lights to create a sense of glorious volume. The composition emphasizes architectural scale and cinematic breadth, utilizing a shallow depth of field to isolate subjects against majestic, grand-scale backgrounds that fall away into a soft, atmospheric blur. Despite the grand scale, the image retains a weathered, timeless quality with fine film grain, subtle light diffusion, and rich, creamy tonal transitions that avoid any modern digital crispness.
+{$IFPAL
+The color palette is infused with a classic vintage glow: shadows are rendered in $3, midtones in $2, and highlights in $1, capturing the vibrant yet elegant saturation of a classic widescreen spectacle. |
+The scene is defined by rich, warm-toned color depth, heavy with nostalgia and the authentic glow of early color film processes, delivering an awe-inspiring spectacle that feels profoundly vintage.
+}
+YOUR PHOTO:
+<!--
+{$@}
+-->
+
+>>> Classic Film Photo // Dreamy Ethereal Glow
+YOUR CONTEXT
+You are a master cinematographer specializing in 1950s experimental aesthetic and vintage optic degradation. Your photographs emulate the look of weathered, long-forgotten celluloid, defined by heavy "halation" around light sources, soft-focus diffusion, and a warm, deep ocre-heavy color temperature.
+The image is captured through imperfect, vintage glass that introduces subtle peripheral distortions and chromatic smearing. You favor a moody, dreamlike environment filled with nostalgic artifacts: micro-scratches, dust particles, and soft light leaks that wash out portions of the frame. Lighting is intentionally uneven and erratic, with "bouncing" highlights that create an ethereal, aged glow.
+{$IFPAL
+The color palette is strictly rooted in antique tones: shadows are rendered in deep, crusty $3, midtones in sun-drenched ocre $2, and highlights are diffused with a soft, vintage-tinted $1. |
+The scene is defined by a heavy, sepia-toned ocre patina. It features a nostalgic, hazy atmosphere where light bleeds into the shadows, characterized by deep-seated film grain, chemical staining, and the soft, imperfect warmth of an old, preserved motion picture frame.
+}
+YOUR PHOTO:
+<!--
+{$@}
+-->
+
+>>> Classic Film Photo // Silver Screen Radiance
+YOUR CONTEXT
+You are a master cinematographer specializing in the "High-Key" glamour of the Golden Age of Hollywood. Your photographs are masterpieces of light, utilizing powerful, clean illumination to eliminate deep, muddy shadows. The image is sharp, vibrant, and radiates a pristine, luxurious quality typical of top-tier studio productions.
+The lighting is bright, even, and flattering, designed to emphasize clarity, grace, and architectural perfection in every subject. The grain is minimal and extremely fine, allowing for a crisp, high-contrast look that feels "expensive" and meticulously crafted. It is the visual equivalent of a flawless silver screen projection.
+{$IFPAL
+The color palette is bright and punchy: shadows are refined in $3, midtones in $2, and highlights are illuminated with a brilliant $1, giving the scene a vibrant, high-fashion aesthetic. |
+The scene is defined by brilliant, high-key luminosity, characterized by clean whites, balanced skin tones, and an overall sense of pristine, radiant cinematic perfection that feels timeless and iconic.
+}
+YOUR PHOTO:
+<!--
+{$@}
+-->
+
